 "header": {
  "subsystemType": "Hrot.Scenario",
  "schemaVersion": "1.0",
  "terrainName": "bt-range",
  "description": "What: CE-4629 / R-4280 feature scenario on bt-range - vehicles and men crossing or cutting walls. (1) 'Kerb Car' and 'Kerb Tank' drive north over a 10 cm kerb (y = 120; hulls roll over a wall panel under 0.25 m); 'Garden Car' drives at a 1 m garden wall (y = 128) and must stay south of it. (2) Three AI bulldozers (TKB 112) are ordered to clear a point of a wall: 'Dozer A' a straight 2 m free wall (y = 149), 'Dozer B' a 2 m wall made of one-metre pieces (y = 185; on this flat range one panel per segment, the multi-panel case of a wall stepping with a slope), 'Dozer Fence' bt-range's own 60 m fence row (y = 70); both free walls span the whole range, so only the cut lets a man through. After 45 s two riflemen are ordered through each A / B cut, to the point beyond it and to a point 2 m aside; 'Fence Rifle' through the fence row; a 'Probe' man per wall is ordered through where nothing was cut. (3) 'Dozer House' is ordered to clear a point of House A's west wall (its three doors Locked) and 'House Rifle' into the west room (103, 104). Judge: see checks.json. Fail: the car or tank held by the kerb, the garden car over its wall, a probe through an uncut wall, a man not through a cut, the room unreached. Check: scripts/scenario-regression.sh tt-dozer-breach"
 },
